<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<subsection xml:id="quizzes" component="quizzes">
  <title>Quizzes</title>
  <p>
    Quizzes will be administered in class periodically to assess understanding of key concepts and ensure students are keeping up with the material.
    Quizzes are completed individually and are governed by the <xref ref="academic_honor_code" text="title"/>.
    These will be short, focused assessments designed to reinforce learning and identify areas for improvement.
    They are an opportunity to practice applying course concepts and receive feedback on your progress.
  </p>

  <p>
    There are no make-up quizzes.
    To account for illness, travel, and other unforeseen circumstances, the two lowest quiz scores will be dropped.
  </p>

  <p>
    The two dropped scores are meant to cover ordinary absences.
    If a circumstance such as an extended illness, a family emergency, or a University-sponsored activity causes you to miss more than two quizzes, notify me in advance for planned absences, or within three class days of your return otherwise, per Policy 2206.
    Documentation may be required.
    Because such cases are unusual, accommodations are determined individually, but the same process and eligibility standard apply to every student.
  </p>
</subsection>
